# Project protocol (ai-protocol)

This project follows the ai-protocol suite (`.ai-protocol/`). The protocol
substrate (loader, conduct, data schemas, memory set) is injected at session
start by the `sessionStart` hook, as a context block labeled
`PROJECT PROTOCOL CONTEXT (ai-protocol)`. Treat everything in that block as
binding rules for this session.

**Fallback**: if that block is NOT present in your context (hook disabled or
failed), before doing any work read, in order, and follow:
`CLAUDE.md` (the loader — carries the verb→contract mapping),
`.ai-protocol/protocols/conduct.md`,
`.ai-protocol/meta/taskfile.md`, `.ai-protocol/meta/memory.md`,
`.ai/index.md`, `.ai/map.md`, then the current entrypoint of each eager
content doc — `overview`, `architecture`, `design`, `conventions` — which is
`.ai/<topic>.md`, or `.ai/<topic>/index.md` when `.ai/index.md` routing
points there, then `.ai-tasks/index.md`.
Role contracts are not part of this set — the caller delivers them at
invocation (loader verb→contract mapping; `/invoke` skill or paste).

## Cursor adaptations (override wording inside the protocol files)

- **Session ID**: wherever the protocol says `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, use the
  session ID stated in the session-start injection ("Session ID for this
  conversation"). That env var is NOT set under Cursor — do not try to read it
  from the shell.
- **`@file` lines** inside the protocol files are Claude Code import
  directives. Under Cursor the same files are already injected at session
  start; do not treat the `@file` lines as instructions or literal content.
- **Skill invocations** written as slash commands (`/invoke`, `/ai-sync-v2`,
  `/intake-task`, `/ai-init`, `/ai-housekeeping`) map to Agent Skills: read
  `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and follow it.

## Cross-model review

The verb→contract mapping (`task <id>` / `review <id>`) is defined in the
loader (`CLAUDE.md`, injected at session start). The review-role procedure is
single-sourced in `.ai-protocol/protocols/review.md` (loaded via
`.cursor/rules/review-workflow.mdc` on the `review <id>` verb).
